    "## 5. Prediction grid and UCB acquisition\n",
    "\n",
    "UCB(x) = μ(x) + β · σ(x)\n",
    "\n",
    "A candidate scores well if the model expects a high value there, or if the\n",
    "model is very unsure and it might turn out high. β = 1.96 sets the balance —\n",
    "higher values push harder toward unexplored regions.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why UCB rather than Expected Improvement?** UCB does not need a meaningful\n",
    "incumbent to compare against, which suits the early rounds here: with almost\n",
    "every observation reading as effectively zero, \"beat the current best\" was not\n",
    "a useful question. The trade-off is that UCB applies the same exploration\n",
    "weight regardless of what has been found, so it keeps pulling outward even once\n",
    "a good region exists."
   ]
  },
