    "## 7. Round-by-round review\n",
    "\n",
    "Rounds 2 to 5 all queried **pure corners** of the search space: [0, 1], [1, 1],\n",
    "[0, 0] and [0.41, 0]. They returned 0, 1.5e-192, 2.3e-248 and −1.3e-124 —\n",
    "nothing usable. The best value is still the 7.71e-16 supplied at the start.\n",
    "\n",
    "The R² above explains why, and the explanation is not the obvious one.\n",
    "\n",
    "The natural conclusion is that β = 1.96 was too exploratory. But look at the\n",
    "fitted kernel: starting from 0.05, the length-scale settled at roughly **0.29**,\n",
    "comfortably inside its bounds. The model is not straining against its\n",
    "configuration. It fitted cleanly and still cannot predict a held-out point —\n",
    "An RMSE no lower than that of simply guessing the average (R² of 0.005) means it has learned nothing usable.\n",
    "\n",
    "That is the real problem. Consider what the transformed values look like: the\n",
    "two meaningful readings sit at about −2.4 and −2.9, while the other thirteen\n",
    "scatter between −40 and −248 with no apparent relationship to where they were\n",
    "measured. From the model's point of view, most of this dataset is\n",
    "indistinguishable from noise at wildly varying magnitudes. There is no surface\n",
    "to learn.\n",
    "\n",
    "With nothing learned, predicted uncertainty is near-uniform away from the\n",
    "observations, and UCB reduces to \"pick whichever grid point is furthest from\n",
    "existing data\". On a 100 × 100 grid, that is always a corner. The\n",
    "corner-sampling is a **symptom of a model that knows nothing**, not a\n",
    "consequence of β being too high.\n",
    "\n",
    "The transform was necessary and correct — without it nothing works at all. But\n",
    "it makes the data *readable*, not *sufficient*. Fifteen points, of which\n",
    "thirteen carry no usable signal, is not enough to learn this surface.\n",
    "\n",
    "Three changes worth making:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Switch to Expected Improvement.** A genuine incumbent now exists, so\n",
    "   \"beat the current best\" is a meaningful question. EI will not keep pulling\n",
    "   toward empty corners the way a fixed β does.\n",
    "2. **Generate candidates from a Sobol sequence rather than a grid.** A grid\n",
    "   systematically places its furthest-from-data points at the boundary, which\n",
    "   compounds the problem above.\n",
    "3. **Spend a round near the known signal rather than following the model.**\n",
    "   The two informative readings sit close together around [0.65, 0.68]. With\n",
    "   R² at 0.005, sampling near them by hand is better justified than trusting\n",
    "   a surrogate that cannot predict anything."
   ]
  },
